% The same albuterol for a beneficiary whose only diagnosis is heart failure
% (I50.9), a code of no group of the article: not reasonable and necessary.
scenario drug_noncovered_diagnosis is:
    claim 1 is for the albuterol.
    the HCPCS code of the albuterol is "J7613".
    the albuterol is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 300.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "I50.9".
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Quantities. Dee: 600 units of albuterol for one month is over the usual
% maximum (465), 900 for two months is within it. Eve, who is on formoterol:
% 100 units of albuterol for one month is over the rescue maximum (78), 70
% is within it.
scenario drug_quantities is:
    claim 1 is for the albuterol.
    the HCPCS code of the albuterol is "J7613".
    the albuterol is furnished to Dee.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 600.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 2 is for the albuterol.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 900.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 2 months.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "J44.9".
    claim 3 is for the rescue albuterol.
    the HCPCS code of the rescue albuterol is "J7613".
    the rescue albuterol is furnished to Eve.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 100.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 4 is for the rescue albuterol.
    the quantity billed on claim 4 is 70.
    claim 4 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the HCPCS code of the formoterol is "J7606".
    the formoterol is furnished to Eve.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "J44.9".
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Two short-acting beta agonists at a time (albuterol and levalbuterol):
% neither is reasonable and necessary; ipratropium beside revefenacin is not
% either, revefenacin is.
scenario concurrent_drugs is:
    claim 1 is for the albuterol.
    the HCPCS code of the albuterol is "J7613".
    the albuterol is furnished to Fay.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 300.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 2 is for the levalbuterol.
    the HCPCS code of the levalbuterol is "J7614".
    the levalbuterol is furnished to Fay.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 300.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 3 is for the ipratropium.
    the HCPCS code of the ipratropium is "J7644".
    the ipratropium is furnished to Fay.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 60.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 4 is for the revefenacin.
    the HCPCS code of the revefenacin is "J7677".
    the revefenacin is furnished to Fay.
    the quantity billed on claim 4 is 5250.
    claim 4 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "J44.1".
    rn expects answers ["claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Cystic fibrosis (E84.0): dornase alfa (group 9), tobramycin (group 10) and
% hypertonic saline (group 15) are covered; pentamidine (group 4) is not.
scenario cystic_fibrosis_drugs is:
    claim 1 is for the dornase alfa.
    the HCPCS code of the dornase alfa is "J7639".
    the dornase alfa is furnished to Gus.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 75.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 2 is for the tobramycin.
    the HCPCS code of the tobramycin is "J7682".
    the tobramycin is furnished to Gus.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 56.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 3 is for the hypertonic saline.
    the HCPCS code of the hypertonic saline is "J7131".
    the hypertonic saline is furnished to Gus.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 240.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 4 is for the pentamidine.
    the HCPCS code of the pentamidine is "J2545".
    the pentamidine is furnished to Gus.
    the quantity billed on claim 4 is 1.
    claim 4 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Gus is "E84.0".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Pentamidine for pneumocystosis (B59, group 4): the drug, the E0572
% compressor administering it and its filtered nebulizer (A7006, one a
% month) are reasonable and necessary.
scenario pentamidine_filtered_nebulizer is:
    claim 1 is for the pentamidine.
    the HCPCS code of the pentamidine is "J2545".
    the pentamidine is furnished to Hal.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 1.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 2 is for the aerosol compressor.
    the HCPCS code of the aerosol compressor is "E0572".
    the aerosol compressor is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the pentamidine is administered with the aerosol compressor.
    claim 3 is for the filtered nebulizer.
    the HCPCS code of the filtered nebulizer is "A7006".
    the filtered nebulizer is furnished to Hal.
    the filtered nebulizer is an accessory of the aerosol compressor.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 1.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Hal is "B59".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Humidity for thick tenacious secretions with a tracheostomy (Z93.0, group
% 5): the E0565 compressor, its large volume nebulizer (A7017) and the
% water (A7018, 18 liters a month) are covered for Ivy, and so is the
% bottle nebulizer E0580 she uses with her oxygen system; Jon, with the same
% diagnosis but no secretions in the record, gets nothing.
scenario large_volume_humidification is:
    claim 1 is for the heavy duty compressor.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty compressor is "E0565".
    the heavy duty compressor is furnished to Ivy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the large volume nebulizer.
    the HCPCS code of the large volume nebulizer is "A7017".
    the large volume nebulizer is furnished to Ivy.
    the large volume nebulizer is an accessory of the heavy duty compressor.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 1.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 3 is for the sterile water.
    the HCPCS code of the sterile water is "A7018".
    the sterile water is furnished to Ivy.
    the sterile water is an accessory of the large volume nebulizer.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 18.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 4 is for the bottle nebulizer.
    the HCPCS code of the bottle nebulizer is "E0580".
    the bottle nebulizer is furnished to Ivy.
    the diagnosis code of Ivy is "Z93.0".
    the medical record of Ivy documents thick tenacious secretions.
    claim 5 is for the other compressor.
    the HCPCS code of the other compressor is "E0565".
    the other compressor is furnished to Jon.
    the rental month of claim 5 is 1.
    the diagnosis code of Jon is "Z93.0".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A complete claim for a month of ensifentrine (J7601, 60 units) for a COPD
% beneficiary (J44.1, group 16) on dual maintenance therapy whose
% exacerbations continue: the finding of the treating practitioner, and the
% documentation the Policy Article asks for.
scenario ensifentrine_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the ensifentrine.
    the HCPCS code of the ensifentrine is "J7601".
    the ensifentrine is furnished to Kim.
    the residence of Kim is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Kim is "J44.1".
    the maintenance therapy of Kim is dual long acting bronchodilator therapy.
    the finding maintenance therapy insufficient about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "two exacerbations with emergency room visits in the last twelve months".
    the medical record of Kim documents continued maintenance therapy.
    the medical record of Kim documents continued COPD exacerbations.
    the order for the ensifentrine is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the ensifentrine is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes order date.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes description of the item.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the ensifentrine was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the ensifentrine was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the ensifentrine.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The same claim without the practitioner's note that the maintenance
% therapy continues: reasonable and necessary, but the policy's own
% documentation is missing — payable fails at the remedy.
scenario ensifentrine_undocumented is:
    claim 1 is for the ensifentrine.
    the HCPCS code of the ensifentrine is "J7601".
    the ensifentrine is furnished to Kim.
    the residence of Kim is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Kim is "J44.1".
    the maintenance therapy of Kim is dual long acting bronchodilator therapy.
    the finding maintenance therapy insufficient about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "two exacerbations with emergency room visits in the last twelve months".
    the medical record of Kim documents continued COPD exacerbations.
    the order for the ensifentrine is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the ensifentrine is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes order date.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes description of the item.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the ensifentrine includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the ensifentrine was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the ensifentrine was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the ensifentrine.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the medical record of Kim documents continued maintenance therapy"]].

% Ensifentrine and the finding. Lee: the Council finds the exacerbations
% unsupported — not reasonable and necessary. Max: nobody has made the
% finding — the answer is conditional on it. Ned: no maintenance therapy —
% not reasonable and necessary whatever the finding.
scenario ensifentrine_findings is:
    claim 1 is for the ensifentrine.
    the HCPCS code of the ensifentrine is "J7601".
    the ensifentrine is furnished to Lee.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Lee is "J44.1".
    the maintenance therapy of Lee is triple therapy with inhaled corticosteroid.
    the finding maintenance therapy insufficient about Lee is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record shows one exacerbation treated in the office, without hospitalization, emergency visit or a new systemic prescription".
    claim 2 is for the other ensifentrine.
    the HCPCS code of the other ensifentrine is "J7601".
    the other ensifentrine is furnished to Max.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 60.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Max is "J44.1".
    the maintenance therapy of Max is triple therapy with inhaled corticosteroid.
    claim 3 is for the third ensifentrine.
    the HCPCS code of the third ensifentrine is "J7601".
    the third ensifentrine is furnished to Ned.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 60.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ned is "J44.1".
    the finding maintenance therapy insufficient about Ned is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding maintenance therapy insufficient about Max is established"].

% Treprostinil (J7686) for primary pulmonary hypertension (I27.0, group 11)
% with the findings and a mean pulmonary artery pressure of 40 mm Hg at
% rest, and the ultrasonic nebulizer (E0574) administering it; the same
% generator administering albuterol to Pam (COPD) is not covered.
scenario treprostinil_ultrasonic is:
    claim 1 is for the treprostinil.
    the HCPCS code of the treprostinil is "J7686".
    the treprostinil is furnished to Ola.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 31.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 2 is for the ultrasonic generator.
    the HCPCS code of the ultrasonic generator is "E0574".
    the ultrasonic generator is furnished to Ola.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the treprostinil is administered with the ultrasonic generator.
    the diagnosis code of Ola is "I27.0".
    the finding qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology about Ola is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "primary pulmonary hypertension, no left heart disease".
    the finding pulmonary hypertension progressed despite treatment about Ola is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of Ola at rest is 40 mm Hg.
    the finding significant pulmonary hypertension symptoms about Ola is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe dyspnea on exertion and syncope".
    the finding calcium channel blockers excluded about Ola is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "vasoreactivity testing negative".
    claim 3 is for the other generator.
    the HCPCS code of the other generator is "E0574".
    the other generator is furnished to Pam.
    the rental month of claim 3 is 1.
    the HCPCS code of the albuterol is "J7613".
    the albuterol is administered with the other generator.
    the diagnosis code of Pam is "J44.1".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Treprostinil for pulmonary hypertension with interstitial lung disease
% (I27.23): criterion 4 — the CT, the pressures, the resistance, the
% symptoms — without the findings of criteria 1–3.
scenario treprostinil_interstitial is:
    claim 1 is for the treprostinil.
    the HCPCS code of the treprostinil is "J7686".
    the treprostinil is furnished to Rae.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 31.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Rae is "I27.23".
    interstitial lung disease of Rae was confirmed by a high-resolution CT scan of the chest.
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of Rae at rest is 28 mm Hg.
    the pulmonary capillary wedge pressure of Rae is 12 mm Hg.
    the pulmonary vascular resistance of Rae at rest is 4.5 Wood units.
    the finding significant pulmonary hypertension symptoms about Rae is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "dyspnea on exertion and fatigability".
    the finding qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology about Rae is unsupported, according to the treating practitioner, because "the hypertension is secondary to the lung disease".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

