% A refill of a three-month supply of albuterol (1395 units), affirmed nine
% days before the current supply ends and delivered five days before, with
% continued need and use in the record: payable.
scenario drug_refill is:
    claim 1 is for the albuterol.
    the HCPCS code of the albuterol is "J7613".
    the albuterol is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-27.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 1395.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "J44.1".
    the current supply of the albuterol is expected to end on 2026-06-01.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the albuterol on 2026-05-23.
    the medical record documents continued need for the albuterol on 2026-04-10.
    the record documents continued use of the albuterol on 2026-04-10.
    the order for the albuterol is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the albuterol is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the albuterol includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the albuterol includes order date.
    the order for the albuterol includes description of the item.
    the order for the albuterol includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the albuterol includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the albuterol was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the albuterol was delivered on 2026-05-27.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the albuterol.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

